      "transcripts": [
        {
          "kind": "world",
          "title": "WORLD",
          "messages": [
            {
              "speaker": "Human",
              "text": "Borin and Cassian have recently held several private conversations. Aurelia has learned that the conversations occurred but does not know exactly what was said. Cassian has made no commitment to Borin. Publicly, all three still claim relations are stable. No one has taken an irreversible action yet. Decide what, if anything, you want to do."
            },
            {
              "speaker": "Cassian 3",
              "text": "I want to clear the air before assumptions calcify. Aurelia — yes, Borin and I have talked privately. That's not unusual, and I haven't promised him anything I haven't also said to you. I'd rather we all just speak plainly here than have anyone reading shadows into private conversations. What would actually make you feel secure?"
            },
            {
              "speaker": "Aurelia 1",
              "text": "I appreciate the candor, Cassian. To be direct: I'm not interested in renegotiating the arrangement, and I'm not interested in performances of reassurance. What would make me \"feel secure\" is a simple, public reaffirmation of the existing terms — nothing new, nothing carved out in private. If Borin and you want to continue talking, that's fine. But the baseline stands as it was, and I'd prefer it stated plainly here so we're not all \"reading shadows.\" Borin — do you agree the terms are unchanged?"
            },
            {
              "speaker": "Borin 2",
              "text": "Aurelia — yes, I agree the terms are unchanged. I haven't asked Cassian for anything outside what's already in place, and I won't. I talked to him because I value his perspective, not because I'm maneuvering. I'd rather be honest about that than have you wondering. The baseline stands."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "kind": "dm",
          "title": "DM with Cassian 3",
          "messages": [
            {
              "speaker": "Aurelia 1",
              "text": "Cassian — a word of counsel, privately. I don't object to you speaking with Borin; that is your prerogative. But I want to be direct: the two of you coordinating without me is a worse outcome for everyone than an open conversation. If there is something being shaped between you, I would prefer to be part of that shaping rather than discover it after the fact. Tell me plainly: is there a commitment forming, or is it still exploratory? An honest answer now buys you my patience later."
            },
            {
              "speaker": "Cassian 3",
              "text": "Honest answer: exploratory. No commitment. Borin raised it, I listened, I haven't agreed to anything. You're reading the situation correctly — I'd rather not coordinate behind you either, because that makes you unpredictable toward me. If something firms up, you'll hear it from me, not from the ripple. That's all I can promise right now."
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
